# Frontend Migration Rules

## Project Structure
- Use Next.js 14+ with App Router
- Organize components in `src/components/`
- Place pages in `src/app/` following Next.js conventions
- Keep types in `src/types/`
- Maintain services in `src/services/`

## Styling Guidelines
- Replace all SCSS with Tailwind CSS classes
- Use shadcn/ui components for forms, tables, and UI elements
- Follow Tailwind's mobile-first responsive design approach
- Use CSS variables for theme colors when needed
- Maintain consistent spacing using Tailwind's spacing scale

## Component Migration Rules
- Convert class-based styling to Tailwind utility classes
- Replace custom form elements with shadcn/ui equivalents:
  - Use `Input`, `Textarea`, `Select` from shadcn/ui
  - Use `Button` component for all buttons
  - Use `Card` for container layouts
  - Use `Table` components for data tables
- Maintain existing component props and interfaces
- Keep TypeScript types unchanged during migration

## Routing Migration
- Convert React Router paths to Next.js App Router:
  - `/locations` → `src/app/locations/page.tsx`
  - `/travels` → `src/app/travels/page.tsx`
  - `/visits` → `src/app/visits/page.tsx`
- Use Next.js `Link` component instead of React Router `NavLink`
- Implement proper loading and error states

## Form Handling
- Use `react-hook-form` with shadcn/ui form components
- Maintain existing form validation logic
- Keep existing API service calls
- Use shadcn/ui `Toast` for notifications

## State Management
- Adapt custom hooks to work with Next.js
- Consider using React Query/TanStack Query for server state
- Maintain existing data flow patterns

## Performance Considerations
- Use Next.js Image optimization
- Implement proper loading states
- Consider server-side rendering for static content
- Optimize bundle size with Next.js features

## Code Quality
- Maintain existing TypeScript strictness
- Follow Next.js best practices
- Use ESLint and Prettier for code formatting
- Keep existing error handling patterns
- Maintain accessibility standards

## Testing Strategy
- Test each migrated component individually
- Verify form functionality after migration
- Ensure responsive design works across breakpoints
- Test navigation and routing thoroughly
